{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Yisrael saw the sons of Yosef.</b> This seeing is with the eye of the intellect, not with the sense of sight, for it is said of him, ״ולא יכול לראות״ — 'and he could not see.' <b>Who are these</b> — who are not worthy of blessing, for he saw Yerav'am who was destined to come forth from the tribe of Efrayim, who set up two calves, of whom it is said (Exodus 32:4): ״אלה אלהיך ישראל״ — 'These are your gods, Yisrael'; and he saw Yehu and his sons coming forth from Menasheh. And Yosef answered and said, <b>They are my sons, whom Elohim has given me בזה.</b> He mentioned the Name that performed miracles for him and brought him to royalty, until the king gave him this woman, and from her were born these sons. And he said בזה, that is, in this matter that I have said — that they were born to me in Egypt. And the Sages, of blessed memory, expounded: בזה — he showed him her marriage contract."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:06.860886848Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}